# caravan_suffice_witness.rish -- Caravan suffice witness.
#
# `apprise.rye` opened the last door: the finding a plan reached is carried to
# the reader who won it, byte for byte, into the box they already know -- and
# then the arc asks that reader nothing.
#
#   THE READER WHO WAS TOLD SAYS WHETHER IT SETTLES THE THING.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, MEASURED:
#
#   * THE NUMBER THE TWO PLANS DISAGREE ON IS ANSWERS A PLAN CARRIED WHOSE WORTH
#     IT NEVER LEARNED. Both runs open holding the same debt an earlier run
#     booked, both carry the same case to the same desk, both read the same
#     hand's answer, both publish the same finding, both take it on the record,
#     both meet the admission and take it down, both say what the look came to,
#     and both carry that finding home to the reader who won it. What parts them
#     is whether that reader is ever asked what they make of it. It falls from
#     1 to 0.
#   * THE WORD IS READ OFF THE WIRE, AND NEVER WRITTEN BY A RUN. A supervisor
#     able to author its reader's satisfaction has graded its own answer, which
#     is the whole thing this arc has spent thirty rungs preventing. So the word
#     stands in that reader's own box, `caravan/.readers/desk.suits`, written by
#     a hand outside the plan -- and `SufficeSilent` refuses by name on metal
#     where that box holds nothing, since silence is no consent here.
#   * THE READER'S OWN WORD IS SITTING IN THEIR BOX UNDER BOTH RUNS. The
#     unasking plan is not blocked from learning; it simply never looks. That is
#     what makes the silence a cost rather than an impossibility, and it is read
#     here straight off the wire.
#   * A WORD MUST NAME THE ANSWER IT WEIGHS. A reader may still be holding their
#     verdict on an earlier look at an earlier admission, and reading that as
#     today's word would credit this run with a satisfaction nobody expressed
#     about it -- so the word carries four bytes, the three carried to them
#     echoed back exactly and one more saying what they make of it.
#     `SufficeMismatched` is the rung itself, refused by name on metal.
#   * TWO HONEST WORDS, AND THE PLAN MAY NOT PREFER EITHER. `settles` is the
#     reader saying the answer closes the matter; `wanting` is the reader saying
#     it falls short. This lap's reader says `wanting`, on purpose -- and the
#     plan still settles `carried out whole`, since a reader's dissatisfaction
#     is a fact an operator is owed rather than a verdict on the work.
#   * THE READER KEEPS THEIR OWN WORD WHERE THEY WROTE IT. A weighing carries a
#     verdict inward rather than moving one, so both stand together: the word in
#     the reader's hand, and the plan's copy in `caravan/.suffices/plan.worth`
#     where an operator opens it. Both are read here, side by side.
#   * A READER'S WORD SURVIVES A PROVISIONING, AND THE PLAN'S COPY FALLS WITH THE
#     ANSWER IT WEIGHS -- proven as its own fold, since a verdict swept every
#     morning would leave a plan forever unable to learn what anybody thought,
#     and a satisfaction standing beside a delivery this wire has forgotten would
#     report a reader content about nothing at all.
#   * WEIGHING IS NOT RE-DECIDING ANYTHING. Both runs settle `carried out whole`,
#     both leave the quarrel standing where its holder left it, both leave the
#     age at 4 and the standing loud, both leave the same case on the same desk,
#     both publish the same finding, both take it on the record, both leave
#     today's own concession owing nothing, both meet the inherited debt and take
#     it down, both say what the look found, and both carry it home.
#   * FIVE REFUSALS THIS RUNG EARNS, matching the five below it. `SufficeUntold`
#     is the moment a word is read at all: a run that carried nothing to anybody
#     has asked nobody anything. `SufficeSilent` is the hard half.
#     `SufficeMismatched` is the whole point. `SufficeMiscounted` is the honesty
#     of the count: every answer carried is weighed or left unasked, never both
#     and never neither. `SufficeMisrecorded` is the record, read back from the
#     note a later run finds.
#   * EVERY RUNG BELOW STILL STANDS, each carried whole. A plan that loses nothing
#     still reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs, this arc's standing
#     generalization test one tier further out.
#
# Six RED paths were proven on metal before this witness claimed GREEN. Skip the
# write and keep the read-back armed and the run refuses `SufficeMisrecorded`.
# Read the delivery as absent and it refuses `SufficeUntold`. Let the reader's
# box read empty while every rung below is satisfied and it refuses
# `SufficeSilent`. Read a word about some other answer and it refuses
# `SufficeMismatched` -- the rung itself. Count one answer as both weighed and
# left unasked and it refuses `SufficeMiscounted`. Disarm every guard at once --
# the write skipped, the read-back dropped, and the harness's own two reads
# removed -- and the selftest calls itself GREEN while
# `caravan/.suffices/plan.worth` does not exist at all, so an operator would
# believe a plan had learned what its reader thought when nobody ever asked.
# Seeing that is what makes the reading back a check rather than decoration.
#
# Checks read the selftest output natively (`contains`), never a shell grep over
# interpolated output -- REDS %76 / %85, the apostrophe loom.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/caravan_suffice_witness.rish

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "caravan/bin/suffice"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p caravan/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/suffice.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]

assert build.ok else "caravan suffice build failed -- ${build.err}"

# The reader this witness runs is built here rather than borrowed (REDS %92).
let read_bin_build = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/read.rye -femit-bin=caravan/bin/read"]
assert read_bin_build.ok else "caravan read build failed -- ${read_bin_build.err}"

# The board declaration the rungs below opened, unchanged.
let published = run ["sh" "-c" "caravan/bin/read caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron 2>&1"]
assert published.ok else "the board declaration could not be read"
assert published.out contains "domains 4 -- channels 3 -- regions 11 -- grants 22" else "the board declaration changed shape"
assert published.out contains "verdict: whole" else "the board declaration did not read whole"

# A fresh start for the stores, the doorbells, this plan's notes, and the boxes
# outside it. Every quarrel, every finding, every debt, and every word this
# witness reads was seated by the lap itself, standing in for the runs and the
# correspondents that met this argument before today.
let clean = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf caravan/.regions caravan/.channels caravan/.suffices caravan/.readers"]
assert clean.ok else "the region stores, doorbells, notes, and outside boxes could not be cleared"

let test = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert test.ok else "caravan suffice selftest exited non-zero"
assert test.out contains "GREEN" else "caravan suffice selftest not GREEN"
assert test.out contains "the reader who was told what the look found says whether it settles the thing" else "the suffice finding did not close"

# The weighing and its five refusals, read straight, before any dependent runs.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: untold, silent, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five suffice refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "the plan tells the reader who won the admission, and reads what they make of it" else "an asking plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the plan tells the reader who won the admission, and never asks what they make of it" else "an unasking plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the reader who was told says the answer settles the matter" else "the settling word did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the reader who was told says the answer falls short" else "the wanting word did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a reader's word carries four bytes: the answer they were carried, and what they make of it" else "a reader's word did not name what it carries"

# The property that makes a read word worth reading, proven as its own fold: it
# outlives the run that read it, and the plan's copy falls with what it weighs.
assert test.out contains "a reader's word survives a provisioning, and the plan's copy falls with the answer it weighs" else "a reader's word was never proven past a provisioning"

# The apprising below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unfound, unaddressed, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five apprise refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "the plan says what its look found, and carries it to the reader who won it" else "an apprising plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a delivery carries the finding whole: the meeting reported on, and what the look came to" else "a delivery did not name what it carries"
assert test.out contains "a delivery survives a provisioning, and leaves the note it copies where it stands" else "a delivery was never proven past a provisioning"

# The redress below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unmet, unrighted, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five redress refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a redress carries three bytes: the meeting reported on, and what the look came to" else "a redress did not name what it carries"
assert test.out contains "a finding survives a provisioning, and falls with the meeting it reports on" else "a finding was never proven past a provisioning"

# The meeting below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unowed, unsettled, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five meet refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a receipt survives a provisioning, and the debt it answers stays down" else "a receipt was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "a plan inheriting nothing meets nothing, and writes no receipt" else "a plan holding no debt was credited with meeting one"

# The owing below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unsaid, unconceded, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five owe refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a debt survives a provisioning, and falls with the concession it carries" else "a debt was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "a plan keeping its own word owes the work nothing, and books nothing" else "a dissenting plan was made to owe the work a look"
assert test.out contains "a plan that says nothing concedes nothing, and books nothing" else "a silent plan left a debt standing anyway"

# The avowing below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unheard, unfound, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five avow refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a word survives a provisioning, and falls with the finding it answers" else "a word was never proven past a provisioning"

# The three endings the rungs below reach by publishing nothing, each on the wire.
assert test.out contains "a run owed no word from anybody publishes none" else "a plan that carried no case out answered a finding"
assert test.out contains "a plan nobody ever pressed a quarrel against is answered by nobody" else "a plan nobody pressed was answered all the same"
assert test.out contains "a desk that has said nothing yet leaves the case honestly waiting" else "a silent desk did not leave the case waiting"

# The reading, the referring, and every rung beneath them, unchanged.
assert test.out contains "the hand the case went to is read back, and its finding published" else "the reading below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a long-standing quarrel is put before a hand that is neither party" else "the referring below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a long-standing quarrel reads where the outcome is read" else "the swelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "an age climbs by the run just stood and never shortens" else "the dwelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a quarrel comes down on its holder's word and on nobody else's" else "the relenting below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads under the quarrel it inherited" else "the heeding below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a pressed quarrel outlives the run that heard it" else "the endurance below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads what its reader says back" else "the appeal below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it writes back to the reader who objected" else "the tidings below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its marks carry the standing of their objection" else "the standing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its word is read beside the reading against it" else "the escort below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its record may hold a disagreement" else "the record below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it hears what its reader answers" else "the hearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections travel" else "the delivery below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections are addressed" else "the amendment below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own judgments answer to a later run" else "the recantation below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a repair still refuses by name: unread, whole, overreaching" else "the mend below stopped being weighed"

# The generalization test the whole arc keeps.
assert test.out contains "a plan that loses nothing reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs" else "an unlost plan did not read as the line handed"

# The weighing lap: one plan run twice over an answer it carried home to the
# reader who won it, with that reader's own word already sitting in their box
# both times. Every number stands still -- the work, the dependents, the
# correction, the record, the escort, the asking, the mark, the telling, the
# position carried forward, the age, the standing, the case, the finding, the
# plan's own answer, the concession, the meeting, the upshot, the delivery, the
# settlement -- and only the weighing moves.
assert test.out contains "phases: 6 unasked, 6 asked" else "the two plans ran different records"
assert test.out contains "dependents: 6 unasked, 6 asked" else "asking a reader cost work it should not have"
assert test.out contains "phases absorbed into a standing dependent: 3 unasked, 3 asked" else "the two plans absorbed different phases"
assert test.out contains "abandoned reach, conferred and never served: 3 unasked, 3 asked" else "the two plans lost different work"
assert test.out contains "phases re-seated to carry what was lost: 3 unasked, 3 asked" else "the two plans repaired different work"
assert test.out contains "standing judgments taken back on this run's own evidence: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the recanting rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readings corrected where they were read: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the amending rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "corrections carried to the place their reader was reached: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the couriering rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "disagreements written into the record: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the disputing rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published words standing beside the reading against them: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the abiding rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing objections put back to the reader who raised them: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the lapsing rung stopped asking under both plans"
assert test.out contains "marks carrying the standing of the objection they quote: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the standing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "raisers told how their own quarrel came out: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the tidings below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readers whose reply to the answer was read back: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the appeal below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "positions carried past the run that heard them: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "a run whose reader still presses dropped their position"
assert test.out contains "inherited positions weighed into the run's own word: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the regard stopped standing under a live quarrel"
assert test.out contains "standing positions left exactly where they were found: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the relenting below stopped leaving the position standing"
assert test.out contains "standing positions this run said the age of: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the dwelling below stopped dating under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing quarrels published where the outcome is read: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the swelling below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels carried to a hand that is neither party: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the referring below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "carried cases whose answer was read and published: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the reading below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published findings the plan answered on the record: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the avowing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "concessions left owing nothing to any run after: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "asking a reader changed what today's word owed"
assert test.out contains "inherited debts this run met and took down: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the meeting below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "debts a plan inherited that the run never met: 0 against 0" else "a measured run left the admission it opened holding unmet"
assert test.out contains "meetings this run said the upshot of: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the redress below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "debts a plan met whose meeting never said what it found: 0 against 0" else "a measured run left its meeting hollow"

# The apprise below, unchanged and still weighed: both runs now carry the finding
# home, so the telling itself parts nothing.
assert test.out contains "findings this run carried to the reader who won them: 1 unasked, 1 asked" else "the apprising below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "findings this run kept inside its own notes: 0 unasked, 0 asked" else "a measured run kept its finding to itself"
assert test.out contains "findings a plan reached whose raiser was never told: 0 against 0" else "a measured run left its raiser in the dark"

# The three numbers this rung moves. Both runs carry the same answer home to the
# same reader, and that reader has already written what they make of it in both
# runs; only whether the plan ever opens that box parts them.
assert test.out contains "answers this run read its reader's own word on: 0 unasked, 1 asked" else "the weighing did not part the two plans"
assert test.out contains "answers this run carried with nobody asked about them: 1 unasked, 0 asked" else "the other half of the count did not close"
assert test.out contains "answers a plan carried whose worth it never learned: 1 against 0" else "the two plans learned the same about their reader"
assert test.out contains "work still standing when the supervisor exits: 0 unasked, 0 asked" else "the two plans left different work standing"
assert test.out contains "the plan, as an operator finally reads it: carried out whole unasked, carried out whole asked" else "a reader's dissatisfaction decided what the work came to"
assert test.out contains "breaks a named turn: 0 unasked, 0 asked" else "the asking run broke an order its author named"

# What an operator reads is what the wire carries. Every note is read here,
# outside the run that wrote it, exactly as each would be read by the person it
# was written for.
let settled = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.settled"]
assert settled.ok else "the plan published no settlement an operator could read"
assert settled.out contains "c" else "the wire did not carry the carried settlement the repair earned"

# The act this rung is the whole point of, read where an operator opens it: the
# reader's own verdict on the answer they were carried, carried home to the place
# the settlement is read. One byte, and it says the answer falls short.
let learned = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.worth"]
assert learned.ok else "the plan never learned what its reader made of the answer"
assert learned.out contains "w" else "a reader saying the answer falls short was published as something else"

# And the reader's own hand, in their own box, outside this plan's wire entirely
# -- the four bytes the plan may read and may never write.
let reader_word = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.suits"]
assert reader_word.ok else "the reader kept no word of their own about the answer"
assert reader_word.out contains "osrw" else "the reader's word did not name the answer it weighs, and what they make of it"

# The delivery it weighs, still standing in the reader's box: a weighing reads an
# answer rather than spending one.
let carried_home = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.found"]
assert carried_home.ok else "an asking run took down the answer its reader had weighed"
assert carried_home.out contains "osr" else "the reader was carried something other than the finding the plan reached"

# The plan's own finding, still standing exactly where the redress left it.
let finding_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.redress"]
assert finding_note.ok else "a weighing run carried its own finding out of its own notes"
assert finding_note.out contains "osr" else "the finding did not name the meeting it reports on, and what the look came to"

# The receipt below it, and the debt it answers, still down.
let receipt = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.met"]
assert receipt.ok else "a weighing run wrote over the receipt beneath it"
assert receipt.out contains "os" else "the receipt did not name the debt this run opened holding"

let owed = run ["sh" "-c" "test -e caravan/.suffices/plan.owe && echo standing || echo down"]
assert owed.ok else "the debt note could not be weighed"
assert owed.out contains "down" else "a meeting run wrote a receipt and left the debt standing"

# The word below it, untouched.
let avowal = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.avow"]
assert avowal.ok else "the plan published no word of its own an operator could read"
assert avowal.out contains "ua" else "a weighing run rewrote the word it was only asked to leave alone"

# The finding below it, untouched.
let finding = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.deem"]
assert finding.ok else "the plan published no finding an operator could read"
assert finding.out contains "u" else "a weighing run rewrote the finding beneath it"

# The hand that wrote it still holds their own word, in their own box.
let answer = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.deem"]
assert answer.ok else "the hand outside the argument kept no answer of their own"
assert answer.out contains "cl" else "a weighing run reached onto a third hand's desk"

let case = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.case"]
assert case.ok else "no third hand was ever handed the case"
assert case.out contains "cl" else "a weighing run rewrote the case it had already carried out"

# And the reader who raised the quarrel wrote no finding, which is the arc.
let unspoken = run ["sh" "-c" "test -e caravan/.readers/desk.deem && echo present || echo absent"]
assert unspoken.ok else "the reader box could not be weighed"
assert unspoken.out contains "absent" else "a party to the argument wrote the finding on it"

# The standing, the age, and the quarrel itself, each untouched.
let standing = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.swell"]
assert standing.ok else "the standing note could not be read at all"
assert standing.out contains "l" else "a quarrel four runs old did not read as long-standing"

let age = run ["sh" "-c" "od -An -tu1 caravan/.suffices/plan.dwell | tr -d ' '"]
assert age.ok else "the age note could not be read at all"
assert age.out contains "4" else "a weighing run rewrote the age it was only asked to read"

let quarrel_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.standing"]
assert quarrel_note.ok else "a weighing run took down the position it never weighed"
assert quarrel_note.out contains "p" else "the position standing over the plan changed under a weighing run"

let regard = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.regard"]
assert regard.ok else "the regard note could not be read at all"
assert regard.out contains "u" else "an answered quarrel stopped standing over the plan's own word"

let press = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.press"]
assert press.ok else "the reader replied nothing at all"
assert press.out contains "p" else "the holder of this lap's quarrel did not read as still pressing"

let address = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.suffices/plan.at"]
assert address.ok else "the plan kept no address for the reader who took its word"
assert address.out contains "desk" else "the wire did not name the place its reader was reached"

let outof = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.outof"]
assert outof.ok else "the raiser of the quarrel was never told how it came out"
assert outof.out contains "t" else "a word that never moved was reported to its raiser as one that did"

# The dependents measure the loss in their own hands, exactly as the rungs below
# left them, and the follower that once spoke for the judgment falls with it.
assert test.out contains "falls as its author declared, holding 1 conferred arcs it never served" else "a falling dependent did not fall holding its conferral"
assert test.out contains "client_b: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 1 conferred, 0 returned, 1 still reachable at home" else "the dependent a conferral was made to did not read it as its own"
assert test.out contains "client_c: bytes differed" else "the follower that once spoke for the judgment came home after all"

say "GREEN: Caravan suffice witness passed."
